{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The wired earbuds feel useful as a compact alternative to my headsets for laptop listening and calls, without requiring a different setup.",
    "The HDMI cable matches my repeated interest in practical connection accessories, although already having one means I would skip another today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Desktop memory, graphics cards and internal drives assume an upgrade project I have not shown; my computer accessories do not establish a need for compatible internal components.",
    "The cable modem assumes I need to replace my internet equipment, while my Ethernet adapter and cables serve device connections. The Echo Dot offers no clear next step for that work.",
    "The Fire TV Stick overlaps with an entertainment purpose I am already exploring through my Raspberry Pi, so I would keep using that setup first."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My gaming headset and keyboard accessories seem to have been taken as evidence that I want to upgrade a desktop gaming computer.",
    "My memory cards and Ethernet accessories seem to have been stretched into interest in any storage or networking equipment, even when the purpose and installation requirements differ."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent choices emphasize connecting devices, organizing my workspace and maintaining equipment; those practical tasks matter more than a broad interest in electronics.",
    "An accessory can match my interests without being needed now: another HDMI cable duplicates something I already have, whereas compact earbuds offer a different way to listen.",
    "Compatibility and a concrete current use matter before I would choose desktop components or a replacement modem."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my interest in useful accessories but too often interpret it as a need for desktop upgrades or replacement equipment."
}"}
